    "inputs": [
      "A planet mesh and a slightly larger sphere for the shell, both centred at the same point; a DirectionalLight3D as the sun."
    ],
    "outputs": "A planet with a thin blue halo on its sunlit limb that turns orange at the terminator."
  },
  "limits": "Single-colour scattering with an exponential falloff, not Rayleigh and Mie integration. The shell must be a sphere centred on its origin without non-uniform scale. Additive, so it cannot darken the planet. The camera must stay outside the shell.",
